    summary: [
      `Ilyin has been chattering about Dunyasha, the pretty maid, all the way to Bogucharovo. After Rostov meets Princess Marya he falls silent. Ilyin notices the change and stops. He can read his commander's face well enough to know that something has shifted. The teasing tone drops away.`,
      `Alpatyich supervises the binding of Karp, the ringleader. Other peasants step forward to help. The machinery of deference, once broken by Karp's defiance, resumes. The estate is clearing itself. Carts are loaded. The household moves toward departure with the urgent efficiency of people who have lost too much time already.`,
      `Rostov helps organize the convoy, sees the princess into the carriage, and watches it move away. His impression of her stays with him and will not quite resolve into the category of 'a rich heiress I happened to rescue,' which is how the episode will be told and retold in the regiment. He thinks of Sonya, his long-standing pledge. He thinks of Princess Marya's plain, grateful face. He grows angry when his comrades bring it up because the anger is easier to manage than what lies beneath it.`,
    ],
